providing a good user experience for  consumers of your api  is crucial this work continues even  after  you've intentionally built your api with  simple and intuitive design  it's also equally important to enable  developers with self-service tools to  easily find  and learn how to use your api so they  can ultimately build their app using  your apis quickly and securely  apigee's configurable developer portal  enables app developers with api  discovery exploration learning and  testing and so in this episode  we will learn more about the developer  portal  [Music]  whether the apis you build are for  internal or external use  the developer portal enables api  developers to  publish your catalog of api products  offer detailed documentation for each of  those products  create an easy app developer onboarding  process  have mechanisms to create an app and an  api  key you can even try out your api  you can also leverage the default  templates or customize the portal's  styling to suit your company's branding  and what's nice  is that it's connected to your apigee  console which centralizes  all your api management tasks in one  place  including api analytics which we will  dive in another episode  now let's take a quick tour from both a  publisher's view at setting up the  portal as well as the consumer's view  accessing the portal in prior episodes  we talked about how to create a cloud  project  enable apigee apis create an evaluation  org  then log into apigee.google.com build  your api proxy  and later bundle one or more proxies  into an api  product now to create a portal from this  same console  visit publish portals the plus portal  button  to create a new portal since i already  have one i will click cancel and use  this one  next you will see the different items  you can configure in your portal  now we added an existing api product by  selecting api catalog  the plus sign in the top corner and then  select an api product  then select next to go to the api  details page you also need to check the  box called published  to be able to be listed in the catalog  next you  need to associate the documentation for  that api product  the format of the documentation is an  open api specification  which is an industry standard in this  demo i already created one for this  simple proxy  you can then add an image and associate  categories  that help make the api searchable on the  portal  then click save once you have added the  product  and published the documentation you can  actually visit the developer portal  to see what it looks like by selecting  the live portal link to launch it this  is a developer portal  that apigee provides to get you started  and to make changes to the pages and  theme  you can return to your portal's  configuration options and then choose a  page for example  get started this will open the page  editor  where you can make changes using  markdown's simple formatting  which is then converted to html to  render the page  in your browser now let's see the view  from an external app developer visiting  the portal  app developers first sign up to create  an account and log in  so they can create an app and get an api  key  after that this is the landing page for  a consumer app developer  they can see all the api products  available and explore their details  i can view those endpoints to understand  how they work and i can actually  execute a call to try it out if i don't  have an api key  i get an error to create my own api key  i visit new app enter app details  and enable the api product i wish to use  and click create now apigee registered  my app  and assigned a key to it which i can  quickly copy  now let's go back into the api product  and test out the key  click authorize and from the drop down  you can see that it knows i already  created an app which i select and click  authorize now i can make a call which  you can see  it points to my demo app inside of my  evaluation org and is using  this product great so to wrap up let's  do a small recap  apogee provides a configurable app  developer portal  out of the box which is publicly  available on the internet  where developers can find your api  catalog sign up  register their app to get an api key to  use with the apis  the interactive api documentation allows  developers to test out the api while  they're also developing their app  if you found this episode helpful  community you can subscribe to learn  about  more episodes on getting started with  apogee's api management toolset  [Music]  cheers  [Music]  you
 

